{
  "chapter_id": "CH004",
  "title": "Priest, Prophet, King",
  "sections": [
    {
      "section_id": "SEC013",
      "title": "The Shadow and the Reality",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "The encounters recorded in the Old Testament were not ends in themselves. They existed for the purpose of foreshadowing something that had not yet come. Each one was a shadow, pointing forward to a reality that would later be revealed.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA041",
            "SRC001250",
            "SRC001251",
            "SRC001254"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC001250",
            "SRC001251",
            "SRC001254"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA041"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000001",
          "provider_handle": "p1"
        },
        {
          "text": "God does not change his mind the way we imagine. What looks like a shift in how he deals with people is not a change in his nature, because he does not change. His purpose in all of this has been consistent: to teach generations still to come how to serve him.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA042",
            "SRC001266",
            "SRC001274",
            "SRC001283"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC001266",
            "SRC001274",
            "SRC001283"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA042"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000002",
          "provider_handle": "p2"
        },
        {
          "text": "There is nothing new under the sun. Human beings repeat the same patterns because human nature itself repeats. Knowing what has already happened in these patterns equips you to manage what comes before you now.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA043",
            "SRC001291",
            "SRC001293",
            "SRC001296"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC001291",
            "SRC001293",
            "SRC001296"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA043"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000003",
          "provider_handle": "p3"
        }
      ],
      "idea_refs": [
        "IDEA041",
        "IDEA042",
        "IDEA043"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "SRC001250",
        "SRC001251",
        "SRC001254",
        "SRC001266",
        "SRC001274",
        "SRC001283",
        "SRC001291",
        "SRC001293",
        "SRC001296"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "SEC014",
      "title": "Three Sacred Offices",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "In the society of the Old Testament, three people mattered above the rest. They were set apart, consecrated, and anointed with oil: the priest, the prophet, and the king.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA044",
            "SRC001299",
            "SRC001306",
            "SRC001312"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC001299",
            "SRC001306",
            "SRC001312"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA044"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000004",
          "provider_handle": "p4"
        },
        {
          "text": "These three offices remain sacred. They have not changed, even though their outward form has evolved. What was once confined to a nation has now become something God has extended into a universal commonwealth.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA045",
            "SRC001319",
            "SRC001322",
            "SRC001326"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC001319",
            "SRC001322",
            "SRC001326"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA045"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000005",
          "provider_handle": "p5"
        },
        {
          "text": "There is a common priesthood that all believers share by experience. But there is also an ordered priesthood, distinct from that common experience, set apart in a particular order of things. We are not all priests in that ordered sense.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA046",
            "SRC001330",
            "SRC001338",
            "SRC001348",
            "SRC001380"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC001330",
            "SRC001338",
            "SRC001348",
            "SRC001380"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA046"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000006",
          "provider_handle": "p6"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is carelessness to claim total equivalence between every believer and those specifically called and ordered to ministry. That kind of leveling misses the order God himself established.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA047",
            "SRC001373",
            "SRC001376"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC001373",
            "SRC001376",
            "SRC001380"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA047"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000007",
          "provider_handle": "p7"
        },
        {
          "text": "The priesthood was the first to carry out the function of teaching, of being a kind of school for the people. This finds its fulfillment in what Isaiah describes: all nations coming up to the house of the Lord to be taught his ways. Isaiah chapter 2 speaks of this, of the purpose for which the nations come to that house.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA055",
            "SRC001563",
            "SRC001569",
            "SRC001593",
            "SRC001565",
            "SRC001574",
            "SRC001596"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC001563",
            "SRC001569",
            "SRC001593",
            "SRC001565",
            "SRC001574",
            "SRC001596"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA055"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000008",
          "provider_handle": "p8"
        }
      ],
      "idea_refs": [
        "IDEA044",
        "IDEA045",
        "IDEA046",
        "IDEA047",
        "IDEA055"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "SRC001299",
        "SRC001306",
        "SRC001312",
        "SRC001319",
        "SRC001322",
        "SRC001326",
        "SRC001330",
